course: dictionary
lesson: 6206
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. A dictionary lists them as numbers, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Read the words around the word first, then decide which meaning fits.
explain: «The next crewed landing on the Moon is planned for the late 2020s, but dates for big space missions very often slip.» Here a mission is a big trip by a spacecraft, not a school task. The clues are Moon, landing and space.
explain: «Her mission is to save the turtles.» Now mission means the big aim someone feels they must achieve. Same word, different meaning. Always swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: A mission is an important job someone is sent to do, often far away.
fact: A mission can also be a trip by a spacecraft, or someone's big aim in life.
fact: «Mission control» is the team on the ground that runs a space mission. In 1970, mission control helped bring the Apollo 13 crew home safely after an oxygen tank exploded.
fact: Informal: «It was a mission» means the task was really hard work.
exercise: Jayden reads «Her mission is to save the turtles.» What does mission mean here? | A school bell | A trip to the sea | A video game level | *Her big aim, the goal she feels she must achieve
exercise: Dad says, «Carrying all that shopping up the hill was a mission!» What does he mean? | He lost the shopping bags | The shopping was sent to another country | *The task was really hard work | He is going to Mars
exercise: In a video game, what is a mission? | *A task or level you have to complete | A kind of game controller | A type of cloud | A player's score
test: The church sent a mission to a faraway village to help people. What does mission mean here? | A school trip | A football team | A kind of bread | *Work by a church to spread its faith and help people
test: What does mission mean in «a rescue mission»? | A type of lifeboat | A shop that sells rope | *An important job someone is sent to do, to rescue people | A long walk in the hills
exam: In «The diplomats' mission arrived in the capital», what is a mission? | A video game level | A rocket that flies to the Moon | A church hall | *A group of officials sent to another country
